# Figures and PDFs are committed here, deliberately. The product of this
# repository is the published estimates and the charts drawn from them, so
# estimates/figures/ and the PDF copy of every figure are tracked the way the
# CSVs are: a reader who clones a vintage tag gets exactly what was on the
# website that quarter. This follows the bayesian-macroeconometrics policy.
# The opposite policy in chan-jeliazkov-2009, which ignores *.eps, *.mat and
# *.pdf, is right for that repo and wrong for this one — there the figures are
# byproducts a replication script regenerates, here they are the output.
#
# So this file ignores only operating-system clutter and local scratch. If a
# file is worth looking at, it is worth committing.

Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Scratch from local runs: run_release.m stages here and promotes out of it
# only once the guardrails pass, so nothing under build/ is ever a release.
build/
